egin{aligned}\nA(S)&=\\iint_D \\sqrt{6}\\,\\mathrm dA\\\\&=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot\\operatorname{Area}(D)\\\\&=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot(6)=6 \\sqrt{6}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e899b91-0bcb-53c0-b9ba-0dacca57ea69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721121} {:answer/id #uuid "6edcc7fd-4354-5faf-89d8-dce0073457ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721124} {:answer/id #uuid "71a90f48-7048-55f4-a98d-d43a5a782bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721125} {:answer/id #uuid "b8252baf-33c3-5c65-8175-b60d26757065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721135} {:answer/id #uuid "f50c191a-f974-51ec-a88f-f732a605194b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e899b91-0bcb-53c0-b9ba-0dacca57ea69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721121} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c3858ea-b17b-5eda-b7a2-4fdd2f96d204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "79f77ff7-c55f-5fc1-866f-fdce1d4ff7fb" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle u + 2,v + 1,2 u - v - 2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $-2\\le u\\le 0$ and $1\\le v\\le 4$.\n\nThe tangent vectors are $\\mathbf r_u=\\langle 1,0,2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf r_v=\\langle 0,1,-1\\rangle$. Use\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization over $D$, use $$\nA(S)=\\iint_D\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm dA\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and form the fundamental vector product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r_u&=\\langle 1,0,2\\rangle,\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\langle 0,1,-1\\rangle,\\\\\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1&0&2\\\\0&1&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\langle -2,1,1\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+(1)^2+(1)^2}=\\sqrt{6}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter rectangle has side lengths $0-(-2)=2$ and $4-(1)=3$, so its area is $6$.\n\nThe area scale factor is constant, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA(S)&=\\iint_D \\sqrt{6}\\,\\mathrm dA\\\\&=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot\\operatorname{Area}(D)\\\\&=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot(6)=6 \\sqrt{6}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02074459-b577-50f0-9d5a-1b5a604d6ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721113} {:answer/id #uuid "114b4d11-a5f0-5812-86ad-2a27192de7ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721114} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac1048b-881a-5509-8f40-c0c2696de699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721116} {:answer/id #uuid "5101cf78-18d8-52bf-a946-57eabf3b7eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721122} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf9dcd1-4b13-5b9e-8633-6990997bceeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf9dcd1-4b13-5b9e-8633-6990997bceeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721137} :answer-field/id #uuid "2afce41f-4012-5e35-a28e-b40854b24caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b496c3d-20fb-516c-9a84-a4308c3ce6e4" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle u - 2,v - 2,- 2 u + 2 v\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $1\\le v\\le 2$.\n\nThe tangent vectors are $\\mathbf r_u=\\langle 1,0,-2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf r_v=\\langle 0,1,2\\rangle$. Use\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization over $D$, use $$\nA(S)=\\iint_D\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|\\,\\mathrm dA\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and form the fundamental vector product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r_u&=\\langle 1,0,-2\\rangle,\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\langle 0,1,2\\rangle,\\\\\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1&0&-2\\\\0&1&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\langle 2,-2,1\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\|=\\sqrt{(2)^2+(-2)^2+(1)^2}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter rectangle has side lengths $0-(-1)=1$ and $2-(1)=1$, so its area is $1$.\n\nThe area scale factor is constant, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA(S)&=\\iint_D 3\\,\\mathrm dA\\\\&=3\\cdot\\operatorname{Area}(D)\\\\&=3\\cdot(1)=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a690dc-219d-5427-8963-b826c0808d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\v\\\\- u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721164} {:answer/id #uuid "2faab276-4afc-5d63-9ddb-02f8b9ae2b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\v\\\\- u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721169} {:answer/id #uuid "64b7c093-84b8-58f8-b902-96fd5cfc2cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- u\\\\v\\\\- u^{2}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721176} {:answer/id #uuid "95c0f326-0414-5044-b435-d94a1f3bb204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\v\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721186} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e779b3-44c4-54cb-98ca-983a688843ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\- v\\\\u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05a690dc-219d-5427-8963-b826c0808d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\v\\\\- u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721164} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc9433b1-1558-5008-81fa-b8fb48768793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3dadde85-a0f0-52e2-a47e-572b1588ea83" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\begin{pmatrix}- u v\\\\- u\\\\v\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "The fundamental vector product is $\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v$, in that order. Hold the other parameter constant in each partial derivative.\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(- u v)&=- v\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(- u)&=-1\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(v)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(- u v)&=- u\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(- u)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(v)&=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent vectors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\begin{pmatrix}- v\\\\-1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{pmatrix}- u\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the ordered determinant:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\- v & -1 & 0\\\\- u & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{1}&=(-1)(1)\\\\&\\quad -(0)(0)\\\\&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{2}&=-(- v)(1)\\\\&\\quad +(0)(- u)\\\\&=v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{3}&=(- v)(0)\\\\&\\quad -(-1)(- u)\\\\&=- u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\v\\\\- u\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3594b27a-3784-5c21-af24-732fe4694743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\1\\\\e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721170} {:answer/id #uuid "a96de0de-a82d-5e2f-86c2-e67778800cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\1\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721187} {:answer/id #uuid "d98ce482-0470-5801-95ec-6b6c5ab086f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721194} {:answer/id #uuid "f0190c6c-4f7a-5858-b5fd-5de1090b17b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2 v\\\\- v\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721196} {:answer/id #uuid "f306ce14-6257-5108-90a9-24fb3df307fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\-1\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d98ce482-0470-5801-95ec-6b6c5ab086f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721194} :answer-field/id #uuid "146fed7e-00d2-5bb6-828b-f88d3cbeae50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5a5a621c-6e57-5fc9-9bfe-1edc49643f69" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\begin{pmatrix}u\\\\2 u - e^{v}\\\\v\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "The fundamental vector product is $\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v$, in that order. Hold the other parameter constant in each partial derivative.\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(u)&=1\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(2 u - e^{v})&=2\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(v)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(u)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(2 u - e^{v})&=- e^{v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(v)&=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent vectors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\- e^{v}\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the ordered determinant:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1 & 2 & 0\\\\0 & - e^{v} & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{1}&=(2)(1)\\\\&\\quad -(0)(- e^{v})\\\\&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{2}&=-(1)(1)\\\\&\\quad +(0)(0)\\\\&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{3}&=(1)(- e^{v})\\\\&\\quad -(2)(0)\\\\&=- e^{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\\\- e^{v}\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd7f190-1113-5ffd-808e-e8b839ed6e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\- 2 v\\\\- 4 u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721165} {:answer/id #uuid "2c917acd-0698-5db4-a6b1-1241e63b5533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\- 2 v\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721168} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe788d9-f9b1-5dae-b965-ccc8710fe608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\2 v\\\\- 4 u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721175} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c5417-c14a-5fb7-8c7c-71d0abd2136e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\- 2 v\\\\- 4 u - 2 v\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721179} {:answer/id #uuid "c21e112c-7b72-5f6d-98ec-57fa64b361b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\- 2 v\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dd7f190-1113-5ffd-808e-e8b839ed6e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\- 2 v\\\\- 4 u\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721165} :answer-field/id #uuid "c08e200d-c996-53a1-9d97-311a3a6efce6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6b7931d6-ba1f-54b7-94a0-71aa113858f9" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}\\\\v\\\\u\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "The fundamental vector product is $\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v$, in that order. Hold the other parameter constant in each partial derivative.\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})&=- 4 u\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(v)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(u)&=1\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})&=- 2 v\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(v)&=1\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(u)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent vectors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\begin{pmatrix}- 4 u\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v\\\\1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the ordered determinant:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\- 4 u & 0 & 1\\\\- 2 v & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{1}&=(0)(0)\\\\&\\quad -(1)(1)\\\\&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{2}&=-(- 4 u)(0)\\\\&\\quad +(1)(- 2 v)\\\\&=- 2 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{3}&=(- 4 u)(1)\\\\&\\quad -(0)(- 2 v)\\\\&=- 4 u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\- 2 v\\\\- 4 u\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15489827-c34c-57ac-82d2-4942a21cdf59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721167} {:answer/id #uuid "5ef49eb2-4dd2-5973-b423-ad7f12f102b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\- \\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721174} {:answer/id #uuid "83460164-36c1-525c-bf75-5c162331d8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721185} {:answer/id #uuid "add6f02a-b730-53e1-82b4-f4d99e73dfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721188} {:answer/id #uuid "de4df2d0-aeb8-517c-b12b-fb1b51c37943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- \\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15489827-c34c-57ac-82d2-4942a21cdf59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721167} :answer-field/id #uuid "7786866b-f658-549f-ad58-7658dddfc642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "70c6b754-45d2-531f-bd84-7fa10363d442" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\v\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "The fundamental vector product is $\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v$, in that order. Hold the other parameter constant in each partial derivative.\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(\\cos{(u )})&=- \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(\\sin{(u )})&=\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(v)&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(\\cos{(u )})&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(\\sin{(u )})&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(v)&=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent vectors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\begin{pmatrix}- \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\cos{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the ordered determinant:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\- \\sin{(u )} & \\cos{(u )} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{1}&=(\\cos{(u )})(1)\\\\&\\quad -(0)(0)\\\\&=\\cos{(u )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{2}&=-(- \\sin{(u )})(1)\\\\&\\quad +(0)(0)\\\\&=\\sin{(u )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{3}&=(- \\sin{(u )})(0)\\\\&\\quad -(\\cos{(u )})(0)\\\\&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44452604-da72-549f-bc6e-36c0713f82b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\- \\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721172} {:answer/id #uuid "749b009c-fd28-5533-9a1b-63f4ca7e4015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721181} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac1cfe4-0b41-5816-8d33-17e6b85c3cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721183} {:answer/id #uuid "81eb0ed9-e7a5-582d-822d-13c7b28ce6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721184} {:answer/id #uuid "c3892676-09a1-59db-9801-bfe6df155afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(u )} - \\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44452604-da72-549f-bc6e-36c0713f82b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\- \\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721172} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c9ed5fa-8d98-5e97-b5c7-ab356d923790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4fce8ee-87ad-56f0-b48b-4738914107b7" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\begin{pmatrix}v \\cos{(u )}\\\\\\sin{(u )}\\\\- v^{2}\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "The fundamental vector product is $\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v$, in that order. Hold the other parameter constant in each partial derivative.\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(v \\cos{(u )})&=- v \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(\\sin{(u )})&=\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}(- v^{2})&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(v \\cos{(u )})&=\\cos{(u )}\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(\\sin{(u )})&=0\\\\\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(- v^{2})&=- 2 v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent vectors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\begin{pmatrix}- v \\sin{(u )}\\\\\\cos{(u )}\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\\\\\mathbf r_v&=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos{(u )}\\\\0\\\\- 2 v\\end{pmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the ordered determinant:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\- v \\sin{(u )} & \\cos{(u )} & 0\\\\\\cos{(u )} & 0 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{1}&=(\\cos{(u )})(- 2 v)\\\\&\\quad -(0)(0)\\\\&=- 2 v \\cos{(u )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{2}&=-(- v \\sin{(u )})(- 2 v)\\\\&\\quad +(0)(\\cos{(u )})\\\\&=- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v)_{3}&=(- v \\sin{(u )})(0)\\\\&\\quad -(\\cos{(u )})(\\cos{(u )})\\\\&=- \\cos^{2}{(u )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 v \\cos{(u )}\\\\- 2 v^{2} \\sin{(u )}\\\\- \\cos^{2}{(u )}\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082bf288-f70a-5a25-a571-cc4b23671f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721368} {:answer/id #uuid "563150bf-b27c-52ec-ae5d-58e9ffb0478f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{2 u^{2} + 9 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721375} {:answer/id #uuid "749f9612-636c-593b-a49a-235f01b14649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721379} {:answer/id #uuid "964bc584-a325-50ac-af87-1a4c26673dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u + 6 v + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721386} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbc9af6-b0d2-554a-8d39-161410363b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{8 u^{2} + 9 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "749f9612-636c-593b-a49a-235f01b14649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a48224-9e5d-5059-afd0-3336161b4ab5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a1c58d3-9453-566c-b385-d2f90c327d54" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\mathrm dA\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 1,\\ 0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} + 3 v^{2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D$.\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The surface-area integrand is the magnitude of the fundamental vector product:\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D \\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate with respect to each parameter:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\langle 1,\\,0,\\,4 u\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v&=\\langle 0,\\,1,\\,6 v\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpand the determinant to find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 v\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\langle - 4 u,\\,- 6 v,\\,1\\rangle\n$$\n\nSquare the components, add, and take the nonnegative square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|^2&=\\left(- 4 u\\right)^2+\\left(- 6 v\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(1\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|&=\\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the required integral is\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D \\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nThe missing expression is $\\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 36 v^{2} + 1}$. The integral does not need to be evaluated."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78dd0932-060f-5a46-83f5-9a76205f844d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2} v \\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721380} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5cb35b-0105-517a-86af-d9d55ce89ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721384} {:answer/id #uuid "98d539da-3e5a-536d-9b56-044668b16698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v \\sqrt{128 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721387} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3dcb21-452b-537f-87ae-606dfa5c8880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{3} u v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721389} {:answer/id #uuid "e6031434-2e8a-5215-9697-777f18923404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v \\sqrt{320 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d539da-3e5a-536d-9b56-044668b16698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v \\sqrt{128 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721387} :answer-field/id #uuid "60633444-4f6a-5b62-82f7-c39e1405afee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70641e01-71d9-52eb-8163-a5a8240b7e19" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\mathrm dA\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 2,\\ 0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle 4 u^{2},\\,u - v^{2},\\,v^{2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D$.\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The surface-area integrand is the magnitude of the fundamental vector product:\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D \\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate with respect to each parameter:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\langle 8 u,\\,1,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v&=\\langle 0,\\,- 2 v,\\,2 v\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpand the determinant to find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ 8 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - 2 v & 2 v\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\langle 2 v,\\,- 16 u v,\\,- 16 u v\\rangle\n$$\n\nSquare the components, add, and take the nonnegative square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|^2&=\\left(2 v\\right)^2+\\left(- 16 u v\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(- 16 u v\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|&=\\sqrt{512 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{2}} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{4 v^{2} \\left(128 u^{2} + 1\\right)} \\\\ &=2 v \\sqrt{128 u^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $D$, both parameters are nonnegative, so $\\sqrt{v^2}=|v|=v$.\n\nThus the required integral is\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D 2 v \\sqrt{128 u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nThe missing expression is $2 v \\sqrt{128 u^{2} + 1}$. The integral does not need to be evaluated."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff8bdfe-6efe-56dd-8cbb-45d17226a9c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721370} {:answer/id #uuid "45d8c06b-caa6-59fb-84d4-cf55e32d7c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721373} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec65959-aa10-5dda-a5f4-36586f18ecf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721382} {:answer/id #uuid "be553c1a-c3e9-5080-8830-b54ad250b00d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721397} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb7f6b2-96eb-590e-ae0c-697b62646f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d8c06b-caa6-59fb-84d4-cf55e32d7c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721373} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eecd500-a651-550a-8abf-930f7d5c5f5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "868432bb-acf3-55dc-b1d7-5e7b570cdb92" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\mathrm dA\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 2,\\ 0\\le v\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(u,v)=\\langle u,\\,v,\\,3 u + 4 v\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D$.\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The surface-area integrand is the magnitude of the fundamental vector product:\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D \\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate with respect to each parameter:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u&=\\langle 1,\\,0,\\,3\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v&=\\langle 0,\\,1,\\,4\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpand the determinant to find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v=\\langle -3,\\,-4,\\,1\\rangle\n$$\n\nSquare the components, add, and take the nonnegative square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|^2&=\\left(-3\\right)^2+\\left(-4\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(1\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|&=\\sqrt{26} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the required integral is\n\n$$\nA(S)=\\iint_D \\sqrt{26}\\,\\mathrm dA.\n$$\n\nThe missing expression is $\\sqrt{26}$. The integral does not need to be evaluated."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09728de0-ebf1-535b-9b22-7b65d95dc60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721369} {:answer/id #uuid "49cb25e4-15e2-59ea-847c-1f5890d65ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{57}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721374} {:answer/id #uuid "afa54371-51cc-572f-8218-b20237fd1f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721393} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d2a12e-78d0-5d1e-b6d4-487aef17ea6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721396} {:answer/id #uuid "d643b68d-cecb-52be-81e8-e4d0d7cf1629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721399}] :